This category lists all [[Enemy Bases]] that are considered their own enemies. Most enemy bases are [[:Category:Typeless Enemies|Typeless]] and have a way to attack the player's cats, though there are exceptions to both. The first animated base that was added to the game was the [[Dummy (Enemy Base)|Dummy]], the enemy base in [[Wanderer's Trial (Stage 1)]].

==Trivia==
*Because animated bases are in reality enemies simulating the presence of a base:
**They have stats that can scale on higher Crown difficulties. This primarily affects base health, but also applies to their attack power, when applicable.
**They are vulnerable to [[Surge Attack]]s (except the [[Origin Base (Enemy Base)|Origin Base]] and [[Parasol Base (Enemy Base)|Parasol Base]]) and [[Explosion]]s (except Parasol Base).
**They count towards the enemy limit.
**They appear in the enemy formation when viewing the enemies in their respective stages.
**The enemy base and the [[Cat Base]] reaching 0 HP on the same frame counts as a victory for the player in stages with non-animated bases, but a loss in stages with animated bases. The player will immediately win if they continue the battle by spending [[Cat Food]] or watching an ad.
*The [[Finale Base (Enemy Base)|Finale Base]] is currently the only animated base to be [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] rather than Typeless.
*Up to [[Version 15.1 Update|Version 15.1]] in EN, [[Conjure|Conjured]] spirits were unable to hit Animated Bases not counted as boss enemies.
**Conjured spirits are still unable to hit non-boss Animated Bases in other versions of the game.
**The bug was fixed in [[Version 15.2 Update|Version 15.2]]. However, this correction led to the discovery of a different bug, causing certain Animated Bases to act in unintended ways (e.g. the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]] in [[Ohno Road]] directly targeting the Cat Base upon entering the stage); once again, only occuring if the Animated Base was not set as a boss enemy.

